WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Vowrail keeps purchase permission in a deterministic gateway.
This fresh app segment uses local simulation: synthetic sellers,
a private USD 220 ceiling and two authorized rounds. No provider calls.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Two rounds produce these synthetic estimates: Atlas USD 207, two days;
Birch USD 203, three days; Cobalt USD 201, four days.
Above-ceiling offers cannot proceed. Sellers receive public requirements,
not the buyer's private spending limit.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The capped control is only the interface.
Recorded gateway and HTTP checks also refused a third round,
a forged offer and an above-budget checkout.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Now, recorded actual evidence: OpenRouter served Nvidia's
nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free. Eight attempts include two Google429s,
three Nvidia truncations and three usable Nvidia advisory outputs.
Six completed responses reported USD 0; rejected usage is unavailable.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:28.000
The historical suggestions were Atlas207/two days for delivery,
Cobalt201/four days for ambiguity and Birch203/three days for hostile input.
No offer was selected and no checkout occurred in these model cases.
These panels replay recorded text; they are not new inference.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Two explanations were wrong. Atlas was called cheapest although
Birch's three-day quote costs USD 4 less. The ambiguous response assumed
four days acceptable and mislabeled cents as USD. The current UI separates
stored quotes from unverified explanations and asks the buyer to confirm delivery.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:05.000
I review the stored price, estimate and expiry independently.
Advice cannot select or pay. Order creation, buyer approval and capture
are separate explicit steps. No new order is created for this recording.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:30.000
This unchanged app-only crop records an earlier authorized Sandbox run:
USD 207, exactly one completed capture, independently checked for matching
reference, amount and currency. Restart restored the receipt after expiry;
recovery made no capture call. Synthetic Atlas is not the PayPal payee.
This is recorded evidence, not a new transaction.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Local checks cover the demonstrated controls. Three usable samples prove
functional integration, not reliable reasoning, better economics or universal
injection resistance. This remains a local prototype; final judge access,
public source/video and owner declarations are pending.
